  "question": {
    "text": "Two black bodies at temperatures $327^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ and $427^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ are kept in an evacuated chamber at $27^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. The ratio of their rates of loss of heat are :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{6}{7}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)^2$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)^3$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{243}{464}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints: Rate ofloss of heat $\\propto\\left(\\mathrm{T}^4-\\mathrm{T}_0^4\\right)$\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{E}_1}{\\mathrm{E}_2}=\\frac{\\mathrm{T}_1^4-\\mathrm{T}_0^4}{\\mathrm{~T}_2^4-\\mathrm{T}_0^4}=\\frac{(600)^4-(300)^4}{(700)^4-(300)^4}=\\frac{6^4-3^4}{7^4-3^4}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{E_1}{E_2}=\\frac{243}{464}\n$$"
  }
}